  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>First step of the reaction involves acid base reaction to form&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>Bu</mi><mo>-</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mo>&#8801;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mo>-</mo></msup><msup><mi>Li</mi><mo>+</mo></msup></math>.This is due to the presence of acidic hydrogen in the reactant Hex-1-yne.</p><p>Second step involves nucleophilic substitution to form a higher alkyne.</p><p>Third step involves hydrogenation of alkyne&nbsp;by using lindlar catalyst to form cis-alkene</p><p><img src=\"assets\\st0088_0e483b63033a.png\" style=\"width: 528px; height: 239px;\" /></p>"
